Looks like you're doing quite well so far.  The first issue to remember
is that you're not going to gain any more levels quickly by killing
monsters, so as long as you don't go deeper than some fixed level (I
usually go all the way down to medusa and then stop), the game isn't
going to get any harder on you.  This is important because it means
that this is a good resting period.  So **SLOW DOWN**.  Take the time
to improve the little things that might make the difference.  Get your
naked ac down to 1.  Train and max out the skills slots you want for
later.  Get holy water and bless things.  Identify (or at least narrow
down) as many items as you can.  Knowing how many charges you have in
your wand of fire or knowing if you have a ring of conflict can save
you.  That's the general idea.  I'll go into more (and maybe boring
detail):

1.  Your AC is only -6.  This is reasonable, but not great.  If at any
point have ~$5000 on you, go and donate for protection.  The time
moving between levels should not bother you (though it can be tedious).
 Get your naked ac down to 1.

2.  To follow up on that - have you cleared out all the vaults?  Never
mind the chance of Ludios, the money in the vaults should be converted
to protection.  Check for vault sounds, "ad aerium", etc.

3.  Did you rob the shopkeepers?  Right now, the only reason to carry
around gems is to get money for protection (then have your dog pick the
gems up on the way out), and to (VERY CAREFULLY) engrave a
semi-permenant Elbereth at strategic locations.

4.  Studded leather is nice, but unless its heavily enchanted, dwarven
mithril will give you better ac and won't weigh that much more.  It's
slow, but I would drag (and NEVER be more than Burdened.  Don't even be
Burdened unless you have a means of escape, and never while fighting)
potential armor to an altar, and try on all uncursed armor in the hope
of an extra point of protection.

5.  This depends on your holy water/ identify situation, but I would
bless all my scrolls of enchant armor and use them to enhance any piece
of armor you're planning on keeping for the ascention run right now.
For example, unless you're planning on wishing for a MR granting
artifact, I'm assuming you're gonna keep the cloak (since the Wizard
can steal your Orb).  Enchant it - it's unlikely you'll find a better
one later (baring bone piles).

6.  SDSM.  You have MR already, so this is a no-brainer, esp. since you
don't seem to have reflection yet.  Not only is it better ac than the
studded leather you currently have, but it will protect you from
possible YASD (sleep ray/floating eye/medusa).

7.  Weapons:  The pick-axe you are using isn't really a great weapon.
A dwarven mattock (large pick) uses the same skill slot and apparently
is the best non-artifact weaponin the game.  Better yet, you *have* an
artifact weapon - so use that instead.  If you are holding out for
Grayswandir (and that's a good idea given that you're an Arch), I would
#twoweapon Snick with a something (a pick-axe is fine).  This will
train your #twoweapon skill (which you're gonna want later on anyway),
and does much more damage (you get +6 from 25 strength X2) once you got
things up to at least basic level.

8.  I hope you're planning to let a pet kill the shopkeeper.  Murder is
frowned on by the gods.  Besides, they're not that easy to kill.  Be
careful.

9.  Might as well clear out the first (home) level of the quest.  There
might be some useful item there.

10. Holy water should be a priority for you right now.  It can enhance
many things.  Dip your unihorn into the right potions (dip something
else first to make sure it's not polymorph) and they turn to water.
Turn your booze to fruit juice.  Dip them all into fountatins (or
better yet - wear water-walking boots and dip them into polls of
water), cancel them, and get your self holy water.  Don't worry about
being efficient.  You can always pray again in 1000 turns.  Remember
that you have the time to fool around.

11.  Assuming you've (almost) maxed out on luck, drop your luckstone
before you pray.  It doens't cost you anything, and I believe it will
lessen the chance of you being crowned.

12.  Bless and quaff all your potions of full-healing.  Save your other
healing potions for a massive alchemy session later on.

13.  Use one of those magic lamps as soon as it is blessed (I would
hold off on the second and use it as a permanent light source).  Get
SDSM.  Think about what else you might want for your ascention kit.

14.  Might want to consider nurse dancing, dishwashing

Be careful, keep getaway items in your main inventory, wand of
teleport, wand of fire, lizard corpse, don't be burdend,etc.

Play slowly and be ready to save and plan if anything  unexpected shows
up.

Happy Hacking.
